<title>YEMEN: Yemen considers setting up a stock market.</title>
<headline>Yemen considers setting up a stock market.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen, together with the World Bank, is studying the feasibility of setting up a stock exchange, a Central Bank official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The studies are still not complete in this regard and we are currently discussing this idea with the World Bank,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>On Monday the London-based al-Hayat newspaper quoted a Central Bank official as saying measures were underway to set up the exchange in the second half of 1997.</p>
